# Files whose exact bytes matter must not change with the platform that checks them out.
# With core.autocrlf=true, the Windows default, git would otherwise hand them over with CRLF.

# The product. clear-audit compares its SHA-256 with a recorded value; a CRLF checkout hashes
# differently and would be reported as a modified prompt (found by running the audit on Windows).
plugins/clear-partner/output-styles/*.md text eol=lf
source/clear-partner.md text eol=lf

# Golden renders are compared byte for byte.
plugins/clear-ui/test/golden/*.txt text eol=lf

# Replies as a model wrote them: test input for Clear Transcript's block cutter, whose tests count
# characters and whose heading rule, like the engine's text, knows no carriage return.
experimental/clear-transcript/test/fixtures/replies/*.md text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary

# Bash and VHS read these; bash refuses a script with CRLF line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.tape text eol=lf
